.TH DANBY-MALARIA 1
.SH NAME
danby-malaria \- coupled human and mosquito infection cycle
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/malaria
.SH MODEL
Sh'=-a Sh Iv+gamma Ih; Ih'=a Sh Iv-gamma Ih;
Sv'=-b Sv Ih+mu Iv; Iv'=b Sv Ih-mu Iv.
.PP
Humans acquire infection from infectious mosquitoes and recover.  Mosquitoes
acquire infection from infectious humans; turnover replaces infectious vectors
with susceptible vectors.  Transmission therefore requires both halves of the
cycle instead of a single SIR contact term.
.SH DISPLAY
Four histories make the phase lag between human and mosquito prevalence
visible.  Human and mosquito totals are each conserved independently.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag any compartment bar.  Tracks set mosquito-to-human transmission,
human-to-mosquito transmission, human recovery, and mosquito turnover.
Space pauses, period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/malaria.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/malaria.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-crossinfection (1),
.IR populationmodel (2)
